[{"id":"nba-predict-q2","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is drawn for you. At each rising edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes the value <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> had just before that edge. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn too. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> one cycle late. At each rising edge it takes what <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> held during the cycle before, not the value <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> takes at that same edge: <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> in cycle 2 is <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> from cycle 1, which is 0, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> in cycle 3 is <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> from cycle 2, which is 1. Since <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> one cycle late, <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> two cycles late.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"two-flops-q2","source":"hdl/level-02/two_flops/two_flops_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"two_flops_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"two_flops_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q1","path":"two_flops_tb.q1","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"]]},{"label":"q2","path":"two_flops_tb.q2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["1","0","0","1","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q2","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"nba-predict-q2-hidden","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 2.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">two_flops</code>, two flip-flops in a row: <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is not drawn. Before this window, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> was 0 for several cycles, so just before the window's first edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> are both 0. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> two cycles late: at each edge <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes what <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> held before that edge. The 1 that <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> holds at the edge starting cycle 0 reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> in cycle 0 and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> in cycle 1. If your answer was <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> only one cycle late, you followed <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>: that is what <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> would do if it read <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>'s new value.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"two-flops-q2-only","source":"hdl/level-02/two_flops/two_flops_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"two_flops_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"two_flops_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q2","path":"two_flops_tb.q2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","0","0","1"]}]},"answer":"q2"},{"id":"nba-order-edge","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"core","promptHtml":"Put in order what the simulator does in <code class=\"nobreak\">two_flops</code> at one rising edge of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code>, and after it.","explanationHtml":"<p>At the edge, the simulator first reads every right-hand side, line by line, with the values from just before the edge. Only then does it change the left-hand sides (lesson 2.2). So the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> reads <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> before <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> changes, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> gets the old value. Nothing reads between the two changes, so in the hardware they happen at the same moment. If <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> changed before the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> read it, as when software runs one line after another, <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> would equal <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>: that is what <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code> does. Between edges both keep their values, although <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> changes at the falling edge.</p>","type":"order","steps":["The line for `q1` reads `d`.","The line for `q2` reads `q1`.","`q1` and `q2` change to their new values, at the same moment.","`q1` and `q2` keep these values until the next rising edge."],"shuffled":[2,1,0,3]},{"id":"nba-find-bug","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"This should be lesson 2.2's two flip-flops in a row, with <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> two cycles behind <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>. But synthesis builds only one flip-flop from it, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> always equals <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>q1 = d;</code> is a blocking assignment: <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> changes at once, so the next line, <code>q2 &lt;= q1;</code>, reads the new <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>, which is already <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> then always equals <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>, and synthesis builds a single flip-flop that drives both outputs. Verilator warns BLKSEQ about this line. With <code>q1 &lt;= d;</code>, the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> reads <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> before it changes, and the chain has two flip-flops again. The <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> line is right as it is.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-02/two_flops_bug/two_flops_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// Two flip-flops in a row: q1 is d one cycle late, and q2 is d two cycles","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// late.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"two_flops_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q1,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q2","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    q1 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q1 takes d","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    q2 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" q1;   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q2 takes the value q1 had just before this edge","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":10,"fixLine":"q1 <= d;"},{"id":"nba-report-collapsed","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">two_flops_bug.sv</code> is lesson 2.2's two flip-flops with <code>q1 = d;</code> in place of <code>q1 &lt;= d;</code>. Vivado built it for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the FDRE row. With <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> changes at once, so <code>q2 &lt;= q1;</code> reads the new value and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> always holds the same as <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>. Vivado finds two flip-flops that would always hold the same value and keeps one, which drives both outputs: the OBUF row counts two. Lesson 2.2's correct <code class=\"nobreak\">two_flops</code> builds two FDREs.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/two_flops_bug/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":179,"excerpt":["8. Primitives","-------------","","+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| OBUF     |    2 |                  IO |","| IBUF     |    2 |                  IO |","| FDRE     |    1 |        Flop & Latch |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many FDRE flip-flops did Vivado build?","answer":"1","numeric":true},{"id":"nba-predict-swapped","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"core","promptHtml":"In <code class=\"nobreak\">two_flops_swapped</code>, the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> comes before the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> in the <code class=\"nobreak\">always_ff</code> block; both still use <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code>. Before this window, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> was 0 for several cycles, so just before the window's first edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> are both 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> is not drawn. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>Nothing changes: <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> is still <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> two cycles late. The simulator reads every right-hand side before it changes any left-hand side (lesson 2.2), so the line for <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> reads <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code>'s value from before the edge, whichever line comes first. With <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code>, the order of the lines would matter, which is one more reason to use <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code> in <code class=\"nobreak\">always_ff</code>.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"two-flops-swapped","source":"hdl/level-02/two_flops_swapped/two_flops_swapped_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"two_flops_swapped_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"two_flops_swapped_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q2","path":"two_flops_swapped_tb.q2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","0","1","1","0","0","1"]}]},"answer":"q2"},{"id":"nba-fill-arrow","itemId":"nonblocking-assignment","role":"core","promptHtml":"Finish the line so that <code class=\"nobreak\">q2</code> takes the value <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> had just before the edge.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>q2 &lt;= q1;</code> reads <code class=\"nobreak\">q1</code> with its value from just before the edge, because every <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code> reads before any left-hand side changes (lesson 2.2). In <code class=\"nobreak\">always_ff</code>, write <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code>; Verilator warns about <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code> there.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/two_flops/two_flops.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":13,"before":["// Two flip-flops in a row: q1 is d one cycle late, and q2 is d two cycles","// late.","module two_flops (","  input  logic clk,","  input  logic d,","  output logic q1,","  output logic q2",");","  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin","    q1 <= d;    // q1 takes d"],"blankLine":{"left":"    q2 ","right":";   // q2 takes the value q1 had just before this edge"},"after":["  end","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// Two flip-flops in a row: q1 is d one cycle late, and q2 is d two cycles","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// late.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"two_flops","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q1,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q2","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    q1 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q1 takes d","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    q2 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q2 takes the value q1 had just before this edge","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["<= q1","<=q1"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The rest of the line"}]